(6173230, 909228, 59267, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Abra:</b></div><hr/><i> Congratulations on the Blue!  Thanks for the explanation to my query.  I can see the sand flat now.  ISO 800 for two hours  did you spend hours removing noise &amp; hot pixels, or is the 7D that good?<br/> <br/>I can only dream of one day getting 30 7''s, and they were bringing your score down :-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>PP was about 5 hours total.</td>', 'Originally posted by Abra: Congratulations on the Blue!  Thanks for the explanation to my query.  I can see the sand flat now.  ISO 800 for two hours  did you spend hours removing noise & hot pixels, or is the 7D that good? I can only dream of one day getting 30 7''s, and they were bringing your score down :-)   PP was about 5 hours total.', '2010-09-27 21:58:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6182549, 908910, 69008, '<td valign="top">This is delicious, and my favorite time of day. <br/>You didn''t post your camera settings with this, so I am just guessing that you were shooting at a high iso.  Try some night shots as iso 100 or 200 and it will help a lot with the grainy look in the lower lighted areas.<br/> I''m a relic from the days of film and chemistry, so I sort of like photos with a bit of grain, but they get hammered in voting here at DPC. <br/>This is well composed, and I am ok with the telephone pole. You made a good connection with the title and the pole.</td>', 'This is delicious, and my favorite time of day. You didn''t post your camera settings with this, so I am just guessing that you were shooting at a high iso.  Try some night shots as iso 100 or 200 and it will help a lot with the grainy look in the lower lighted areas. I''m a relic from the days of film and chemistry, so I sort of like photos with a bit of grain, but they get hammered in voting here at DPC. This is well composed, and I am ok with the telephone pole. You made a good connection with the title and the pole.', '2010-10-06 00:15:05.000000', NULL, 0),
